# Environment, credentials, and secrets
#
# Never commit credentials. CI/CD secrets belong in GitHub Actions secrets or
# environments (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions); workflow files
# reference them as ${{ secrets.NAME }} and must not contain values.
# Ignoring a file does not remove it once committed: if a secret was ever
# pushed, revoke and rotate it first, then remove it from history.
# To commit a file one of these patterns would block (for example a public CA
# certificate), add a narrow exception such as `!certs/public-ca.pem`.

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
.envrc

